  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "p-B11 fusion can be made viable through nonthermal proton distributions that suppress bremsstrahlung losses below fusion power production",
      "Alpha channeling via RF waves can extract energy from fusion-born helium ions and redirect it to fuel protons, reducing required confinement time by up to 6.9×",
      "Centrifugal species separation in a rotating plasma can differentially confine boron (11 amu) while allowing helium ash (4 amu) to migrate for extraction",
      "Ponderomotive barriers (one-way RF walls) can control ion traffic between fusion and heat exchange chambers in the multi-chamber CHARM architecture",
      "Direct energy conversion of plasma rotational kinetic energy can replace conventional thermal cycle for electricity generation",
      "A biased central electrode can sustain plasma rotation with large voltage drops at minimal dissipation, keeping recirculating power economical",
      "The integrated multi-chamber architecture (fusion chamber + heat exchange chamber + plug) can operate simultaneously with all five physics mechanisms working together"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "Tritium breeding blanket and tritium handling infrastructure (~$35M tritium startup eliminated; aneutronic p-B11 fuel cycle)",
      "Lithium-6 enrichment supply chain and CANDU reactor dependence eliminated",
      "Neutron shielding, first-wall neutron damage materials (tungsten, ODS steels), and remote handling infrastructure eliminated by near-aneutronic fuel",
      "Conventional thermal power conversion island reduced/replaced by direct energy conversion of charged particle energy",
      "Component activation and associated decommissioning radioactivity costs largely eliminated"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Boron-11 enrichment to fusion-grade purity (>99% B-11 from natural 80% abundance) — specialty isotopic purification",
      "Alpha channeling RF antenna system: high-power ICRF hardware tuned to rotating plasma geometry with no industrial precedent",
      "Biased central electrode capable of ~100 kV sustained operation against plasma erosion and resistive losses",
      "Rotation-energy direct energy conversion hardware (adiabatic DEC or SWDEC) — no prior production design exists",
      "Continuous recirculating power to sustain E×B plasma rotation via the biased electrode system"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Bremsstrahlung losses at p-B11 operating temperatures (~150–300 keV) may exceed fusion power production if nonthermal proton distribution thermalizes or alpha channeling efficiency is insufficient — existential physics constraint",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Alpha channeling efficiency η_α has only analytical/0D model estimates; a 2× shortfall vs. predicted value could make the concept non-igniting regardless of engineering optimization",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Helium ash accumulation could poison the plasma; the multi-chamber architecture solving this has never been built or tested at any scale",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Recirculating power fraction to sustain plasma rotation is uncharacterized; could consume an unacceptable share of fusion output",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "DEC efficiency for rotation energy recovery has only physics-limit bounds (PRX Energy 2025); no engineering efficiency target, prototype, or capital cost estimate exists",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "No published plant design, fusion power, Q, machine size, or magnet specifications — every system parameter must be assumed for any LCOE estimate",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "CHARM multi-chamber integrated architecture is at TRL 1; no proof-of-concept experiment of even a single chamber in relevant plasma regime",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Ponderomotive barriers have high energy cost identified as 'situational' — energy budget for maintaining one-way RF walls at steady state unresolved",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "p-B11 nonthermal plasma has never been demonstrated at any scale (>100 keV proton temperature with cold electrons and measurable yield above bremsstrahlung)",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Pre-incorporation company status (as of July 2025) with only $1.5M ARPA-E funding disclosed; no FIA listing, device roadmap, or independent funding announcement",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Magnet conductor technology, field strength, and mirror ratio unspecified — supply chain and capital cost cannot be quantified without a design point",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Central electrode material lifetime under ~100 kV plasma erosion, sputtering, and contamination is uncharacterized",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Centrifugal species separation at the p vs. B-11 mass ratio in a fusion-relevant plasma has not been experimentally demonstrated; CMFX validates geometry only with D-D fuel at low temperature",
        "severity": "medium"
      }
    ]
  },
